SUMMARY:Ray Lau LIVE at Punch Line Comedy Club Sacramento
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout Ray Lau\nRay Lau is a stand-up comedian known for his sharp\, self-deprecating humor and clever observations about life\, culture\, and identity. His comedy blends personal storytelling with astute social commentary\, delivered with a warm\, engaging style that resonates with audiences everywhere. \nHe has performed at comedy clubs and festivals across the country\, building a loyal following through his relatable and consistently funny material. Fans can expect a polished\, entertaining set full of genuine laughs. \nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\, August 27\, 2026\nTime: 7:30 PM (Doors open at 6:30 PM)\nVenue: Punch Line Comedy Club – Sacramento\nAddress: 2100 Arden Way\, Sacramento\, CA 95825\nAge Restriction: 18+ / 2 Beverage Minimum \nAbout the Venue\nPunch Line Comedy Club Sacramento is Northern California’s most celebrated comedy destination. Located at 2100 Arden Way\, this intimate club has been a cornerstone of the Sacramento comedy scene for decades. \nThe venue features general admission and preferred premium seating\, a full bar\, and the classic two-drink minimum. The cozy room ensures every audience member gets an up-close\, personal experience. Parking is available in the adjacent shopping center lot. \nWhat to Expect\nThis is a solo headline stand-up performance by Ray Lau. Multiple shows are available August 27–29\, so check for your preferred date and time. Expect an evening of sharp\, engaging comedy in an intimate club setting. Shows run approximately 75–90 minutes. \nTicket Information\nTickets range from approximately $46 – $68 (all-in pricing\, fees included before taxes). \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
