SUMMARY:Roy Wood Jr. LIVE at Blue Note Hawaii (Late Show)
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nRoy Wood Jr. is one of the most versatile and celebrated comedians working today. An Emmy-nominated comedian\, documentary producer\, WGA-nominated writer\, actor\, and radio personality\, Wood Jr. is best known for his eight years as a correspondent on Comedy Central’s Emmy-winning The Daily Show (2015–2023). \nIn 2023\, he guest hosted The Daily Show and headlined the White House Correspondents’ Dinner to its highest ratings since 2017. His fourth stand-up special\, Lonely Flowers\, premiered on Hulu on January 17\, 2025\, earning widespread critical acclaim. He is also the host of CNN’s Have I Got News for You\, an American adaptation of the long-running UK comedy series. \nWood Jr. recently released his debut memoir The Man of Many Fathers with Crown Publishing (October 2025) and will appear alongside Keanu Reeves and Jonah Hill in the upcoming comedy film Outcome. Forbes has called him “One of comedy’s best journalists\,” and Variety named him “One of 10 Comics to Watch.” \nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\, August 27\, 2026 \nShow Time: 8:30 PM HST (Doors open at 8:00 PM) \nVenue: Blue Note Hawaii\, 2335 Kalakaua Avenue\, Honolulu\, HI 96815 \nAge Restriction: 18+ Event — Valid photo ID required at entry \nContent Warning: Adult language and mature themes \nAbout the Venue\nBlue Note Hawaii is Honolulu’s most celebrated intimate live entertainment venue\, located at 2335 Kalakaua Avenue in the heart of Waikiki. As part of the iconic Blue Note Jazz Club brand\, this venue has hosted some of the world’s greatest performers in an atmosphere that blends tropical island charm with sophisticated nightlife. \nThe venue offers communal seating on a first come\, first served basis — arriving early is strongly recommended to secure the best seats. A full bar and complete dinner menu are available throughout the show\, with a $20 food or beverage minimum per person. The intimate layout ensures excellent sightlines from virtually every seat in the house. \nBlue Note Hawaii’s warm\, inviting atmosphere makes it the perfect setting for an evening of world-class comedy. Parking is available throughout the Waikiki area\, with multiple nearby garages and street parking options within easy walking distance. \nWhat to Expect\nThis late-night show features Roy Wood Jr. performing his signature brand of sharp\, socially observant stand-up comedy. Known for his charismatic delivery and thought-provoking material\, Wood Jr. blends current events\, personal storytelling\, and razor-sharp wit into a seamless and unforgettable performance. \nAudiences can expect a polished\, high-energy set from one of comedy’s most respected voices. Wood Jr.’s material is both hilarious and insightful — the kind of comedy that makes you laugh and think at the same time. This is a rare opportunity to see a major comedy headliner in an intimate club setting in Hawaii. \nSeating is communal and first come\, first served. Arrive early to enjoy dinner and drinks before the show. This is an 18+ event — please bring valid photo ID. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $45.90 – $56.67 (includes fees and taxes) \n\nPremium Seating: $45 + fees\nLoge Seating & Bar Area: $35 + fees\n\nTickets are limited to 6 per order. No refunds or exchanges — all sales are final. This event is 18 and over. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/roy-wood-jr-live-at-blue-note-hawaii-late/
LOCATION:Blue Note Hawaii\, 2335 Kalakaua Avenue\, Honolulu\, HI\, 96815\, United States
