a $20 food or beverage minimum per person. The intimate layout ensures excellent sightlines from virtually every seat in the house. \nBlue Note Hawaii’s warm\, inviting atmosphere makes it the perfect setting for an evening of world-class comedy. Parking is available throughout the Waikiki area\, with multiple nearby garages and street parking options within easy walking distance. \nWhat to Expect\nThis early Friday evening show features Roy Wood Jr. performing his signature brand of sharp\, socially observant stand-up comedy. Known for his charismatic delivery and thought-provoking material\, Wood Jr. blends current events\, personal storytelling\, and razor-sharp wit into a seamless and unforgettable performance. \nAudiences can expect a polished\, high-energy set from one of comedy’s most respected voices. Wood Jr.’s material is both hilarious and insightful — the kind of comedy that makes you laugh and think at the same time. This is a rare opportunity to see a major comedy headliner in an intimate club setting in Hawaii. \nDoors open at 5:00 PM\, giving you plenty of time to settle in\, enjoy a full dinner from the menu\, and grab drinks before the show begins. Seating is communal and first come\, first served — arrive early for the best spots. This is an 18+ event — please bring valid photo ID. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $45.90 – $56.67 (includes fees and taxes) \n\nPremium Seating: $45 + fees\nLoge Seating & Bar Area: $35 + fees\n\nTickets are limited to 6 per order. No refunds or exchanges — all sales are final. This event is 18 and over. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
