SUMMARY:Francisco Ramos LIVE at Punch Line Houston
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nFrancisco Ramos is a bilingual stand-up comedian who has been making audiences laugh across the United States with his unique blend of English and Spanish comedy. Known for his high-energy performances and sharp cultural observations\, Ramos has built a devoted following among Latino audiences and comedy fans of all backgrounds. \nHis comedy draws from his experiences growing up in a Latino household\, navigating two cultures\, and the universal absurdities of family life. Francisco has a natural charisma on stage that makes his shows feel like a party — energetic\, inclusive\, and genuinely funny. \nHe has performed at top venues including the Arlington Drafthouse\, Desert Ridge Improv in Phoenix\, and now brings his show to Punch Line Houston for a weekend run. His Thursday Spanish-language show (En Español) on August 27 and his Friday/Saturday English shows on August 28-29 offer something for everyone. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Friday\, August 28\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM (Doors open at 6:00 PM)\nVenue: Punch Line Houston\nAddress: 1204 Caroline Street\, Houston\, TX 77002\nAge Restriction: 18+ (2 Beverage Minimum per person)\nTicket Prices: $38 – $50 (fees included)\n\nAbout the Venue\nPunch Line Houston is the premier comedy club in downtown Houston\, located at 1204 Caroline Street. This Live Nation-operated venue is the city’s top destination for national stand-up comedy acts\, offering an intimate setting that brings you up close to the performers. \nThe club features a general admission floor with preferred seating upgrades available. The full bar and 2-beverage minimum per person create a fun\, social atmosphere that enhances the comedy experience. Every seat in the house offers a great view of the stage. \nParking is available via valet service (at most shows) or the Green Street garage on Clay between Main and Fannin\, which connects to the venue via skybridge. The club is cashless — all major credit and debit cards are accepted. \nWhat to Expect\nFrancisco Ramos delivers a high-energy\, crowd-pleasing performance that blends sharp observational humor with cultural storytelling. His Friday night show is the perfect way to close out August with a night of genuine laughs. \nDoors open at 6:00 PM\, so arrive early to grab your seats and get your first round in before the show starts at 7:00 PM. A late show at 9:15 PM is also available on Saturday August 29. The performance runs approximately 90 minutes. \nNote: A special Spanish-language show (En Español) is also available on Thursday August 27 at 7:30 PM for Spanish-speaking audiences. All shows are 18+ with a 2-beverage minimum. No cell phones or recording permitted during the performance. \nTicket Information\nTickets are priced from $38 to $50 (all-in pricing\, fees included before taxes). Purchase official tickets through Ticketmaster or find resale options on VividSeats. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
